WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.168
The next day the rain was still pouring down, and the moor was hidden in mist.

2
00:00:08.169 --> 00:00:11.554
It was not a good day for going outdoors.

3
00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:16.705
Mary had to wait until afternoon to talk to Martha, who was busy working.

4
00:00:16.706 --> 00:00:19.986
At last Martha came to Mary's room.

5
00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:24.525
The two girls sat by the fire, and Martha took out her knitting.

6
00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:28.818
"I've found out what that crying was," Mary announced.

7
00:00:28.819 --> 00:00:33.820
Martha let her knitting fall on her lap. "You haven't!"

8
00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:35.423
"I heard it last night.

9
00:00:35.424 --> 00:00:39.655
When I got up to see where it was coming from, I met Colin."

10
00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:47.658
"Oh no! Everyone will think I told you where he is." Martha started to cry.

11
00:00:47.659 --> 00:00:53.590
"I'll lose my job here, and what will Mother do? We need my wages!"

12
00:00:53.591 --> 00:00:57.341
"You won't lose your job. We talked and talked.

13
00:00:57.342 --> 00:01:00.798
He showed me the picture of his mother, and I sang him to sleep.

14
00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:03.081
I think he liked me."

15
00:01:03.082 --> 00:01:05.759
Martha could not believe this.

16
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.728
Colin was a bad-tempered, spoiled boy who didn't like anyone.

17
00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:13.836
"You must have bewitched him!"

18
00:01:13.837 --> 00:01:19.811
Mary shook her head. "I heard about magic in India, but I can't make any.

19
00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:25.136
He seems to believe he's dying. Do you think he'll really die?"

20
00:01:25.137 --> 00:01:31.675
"Mother says all children need fresh air," Martha stated, picking up her knitting again.

21
00:01:31.676 --> 00:01:38.853
"But all that boy does is lie in bed all day, looking at books and taking medicine."

22
00:01:38.854 --> 00:01:41.510
Mary stared at the fire.

23
00:01:41.511 --> 00:01:49.675
"I wonder," she said slowly, "if it would do him good to go out into a garden and watch things growing.

24
00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.040
I know it did me good."

25
00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:56.713
Before Martha could answer, a bell rang, and she stood up.

26
00:01:56.714 --> 00:02:02.079
"That's probably his nurse wanting me to sit with him."

27
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.028
Martha returned in a few minutes. "Well, you have bewitched him.

28
00:02:08.029 --> 00:02:11.873
He's sitting up on his sofa with his picture books.

29
00:02:11.874 --> 00:02:17.754
He told the nurse to stay away until six o'clock, and he wants you to come see him."

30
00:02:17.755 --> 00:02:21.287
Mary followed Martha to Colin's room.

31
00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:28.062
She was surprised that the room looked so beautiful in the daylight and that Colin looked less pale.

32
00:02:28.063 --> 00:02:34.055
"Come here," he said after Martha left. "I've been thinking of you today."

33
00:02:34.056 --> 00:02:41.612
"I've been thinking of you too." Mary told him how afraid Martha was that she would lose her job.

34
00:02:41.613 --> 00:02:44.555
"Tell her to come here."

35
00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:49.957
Mary went into the next room and brought back a very frightened Martha.

36
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:55.372
"Must everyone in this house do as I please?" Colin asked her sternly.

37
00:02:55.373 --> 00:02:58.595
"Yes, sir," said Martha.

38
00:02:58.596 --> 00:03:03.795
"Then if I order you to bring Mary to me, no one can send you away."

39
00:03:03.796 --> 00:03:07.795
"No, sir. I just want to do my duty, sir."

40
00:03:07.796 --> 00:03:14.075
"I want you to do your duty too. I'll take care of you. Now go away."

41
00:03:14.076 --> 00:03:17.804
Martha curtsied and left the room.

42
00:03:17.805 --> 00:03:22.090
"Why are you looking at me like that?" Colin demanded of Mary.

43
00:03:22.091 --> 00:03:26.891
"One time I saw a boy who was a rajah, an Indian prince.

44
00:03:26.892 --> 00:03:30.457
He spoke to his people just as you spoke to Martha.

45
00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:34.492
If they didn't instantly obey him, they would have been killed.

46
00:03:34.493 --> 00:03:37.275
You are so different from Dickon."

47
00:03:37.276 --> 00:03:40.455
"Dickon? Who's that?"

48
00:03:40.456 --> 00:03:47.555
Mary told him all about Martha's brother and how he charmed the birds and animals with his music.

49
00:03:47.556 --> 00:03:51.626
"He knows about everything that grows or lives on the moor."

50
00:03:51.627 --> 00:03:55.248
"Oh, how can he like that dreary moor?"

51
00:03:55.249 --> 00:03:59.919
Mary protested. "It's the most beautiful place.

52
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.551
I didn't like it at first, but now I do.

53
00:04:03.552 --> 00:04:07.071
You might even like it if you could go out."

54
00:04:07.072 --> 00:04:11.099
"How could I go out on the moor? I'm going to die."

55
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.915
"I don't like talking about dying.

56
00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:17.903
Let's talk about Dickon and then we'll look at your picture books."

57
00:04:17.904 --> 00:04:21.664
"There's one thing we haven't talked about—we're cousins!"

58
00:04:21.665 --> 00:04:31.103
For a few hours, the two children talked and laughed like ordinary ten year olds.

59
00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:37.170
Suddenly the door opened, and in walked Dr. Craven and Mrs. Medlock.

60
00:04:37.171 --> 00:04:43.341
Dr. Craven looked startled. "What's going on here?" he asked.

61
00:04:43.342 --> 00:04:49.061
"Oh, I don't know how this happened!" Mrs. Medlock was flustered.

62
00:04:49.062 --> 00:04:53.557
Colin explained how Mary had found him the night before.

63
00:04:53.558 --> 00:04:57.617
"And now we will have our tea here together."

64
00:04:57.618 --> 00:05:01.355
Dr. Craven did not look pleased at that news.

65
00:05:01.356 --> 00:05:05.060
But he didn't dare oppose his young patient.

66
00:05:05.061 --> 00:05:08.744
"I'm afraid you've had too much excitement today."

67
00:05:08.745 --> 00:05:14.065
"I'm better today," Colin said firmly. "Mary makes me better."

68
00:05:14.066 --> 00:05:21.573
Mrs. Medlock and Dr. Craven looked at each other in a troubled way, but there wasn't anything they could do.

69
00:05:21.574 --> 00:05:25.773
Still Dr. Craven was full of warnings for Colin:

70
00:05:25.774 --> 00:05:31.928
"Don't talk too much, don't forget you are ill, and don't forget you tire easily."

71
00:05:31.929 --> 00:05:38.184
Colin stared hard at Dr. Craven. "I want to forget those things.

72
00:05:38.185 --> 00:05:42.223
Mary makes me forget, and that's why I want her here."

73
00:05:42.224 --> 00:05:50.488
Dr. Craven looked very unhappy when he left the room.

